{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.729403Z","id":"7bec3684a53d4d228891f147137a443ef36e11d906cba05a2696681207c4cf0e","body":{"detail":"frameLoaded() closes the gate on a load with no hello, calls leaveDocument() (host.leave()), and asks the page to greet again with clax:greet. The page's hello reopens the gate, but the capability host starts over, so everything the page had set up through it ends and the page must set it up again. The spec states this as an open limitation (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-28-clax-design.md:1167-1171).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":624},"end":{"line":642},"content_hash":"72305be614779699d14d6ef0e341ca8695bf7df61efd86ed49f766a51dfdd6f9"},"suggested_fix":"When the hello that answers clax:greet comes from the same document (same artifact, version and file), keep or re-establish the host's room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors instead of starting over.","summary":"Back or Forward across a page's own fragments drops its room joins, db subscriptions, sample streams and custom anchors","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/frame-host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730281Z","id":"4d1b4269e54dea08437973adcfaa170940e1002bace91f85d9601704550dd67a","body":{"detail":"With the viewer's activation, a subdomain-mode page can navigate the top window to another site or a fresh Clax load (docs/contract.md, Known limitations). Every load starts with the keyboard trail tainted, so what remains is C and ? live in the fresh load, and the navigation itself. Giving this frame sandbox='allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-forms allow-modals allow-popups allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox allow-downloads' (no top navigation) would stop a navigation to another site; it needs every capability and page link checked first, and a popup the page opens keeps the shell's live keys either way. Decision needed: sandbox the subdomain frame or not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":61},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"431b45f7af17766e5236279b541ce64c1c05c8e23949fa4e3cd7257ec710cfa5"},"summary":"The subdomain-mode frame has no sandbox, so a page can navigate the whole window","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/trail.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730318Z","id":"2ae15dfc4b730f67ed2966a0113bcaa47b3ecf806ab2b2d73e3ad65874f37bea","body":{"detail":"No key clears the tainted trail, and every load starts tainted, so keyboard-only and screen-reader viewers need a pointer for Send, Resolve, Reply, the batch sends, a page-opened composer's Post, and the prompt's Allow. A path a page cannot coax (for example: the control held focus for ALLOW_DELAY_MS with no other key in between) would restore keyboard use. Decision needed: add such a path or not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":50},"content_hash":"6f6b435ae268b57cdf1b57ffc3db1fed62b7b5ee97e1f5ee6deedc2734083c92"},"summary":"No keyboard path for consequential actions once the trail is tainted","tags":["status:needs-decision","security","a11y","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/deltas.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731087Z","id":"3840a663992442d3b8d393dbb11a44ad1af9839c853aa64d6b44e0a1fa87264b","body":{"detail":"The artifact:<id> topic carries a thread's newest comment and its count; a view that missed a comment, or holds one deleted or edited before the newest, gets complete false and fetches that thread whole.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":29},"content_hash":"dde23580758adb5c4ed4da369bdac4d1fbbfe066c2e5b056c20725d2c2610604"},"summary":"A thread delta whose comments do not add up fetches the thread whole","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731122Z","id":"93f0d25e0a13aee591cc4816b13d291787bc44c99eb625e669d011e2d9bbc274","body":{"detail":"A page's own publish (artifact.publish) moves every open unpinned view to the new version when the view hears its version event, which carries by_page (lines 115-128). A view whose stream goes live only after that publish learns of the version from this refetch on ready, which cannot tell who published, and offers Reload in the top bar. The browser tests wait for each view's stream before a vote (streamLive in web/e2e/fixtures.ts:203).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":148},"end":{"line":153},"content_hash":"a91a85289e6e1f0f950c25198984f37c048a7650c830e9460e903fe262484c32"},"summary":"A view that missed a page's publish offers Reload rather than following it","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731329Z","id":"76a00f1b49d5b22fa1e7deb61eece0b7ae52086b335bcdb05f2bc760a5b46906","body":{"detail":"After clax:degraded, the shell holds the part failed for that page: Comment stays off and says so, even once the bridge's own retry could load the part, and threads whose anchors went unanswered while it failed stay unplaced. This needs a protocol addition.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1233},"end":{"line":1243},"content_hash":"d916958d7195a5a877a49f0b9d1b6e048afccef5dc947da03e0bf784247f5cbe"},"suggested_fix":"Have the bridge report a part that loads after failing; the shell then clears failedParts for it and its notice, and resolves the anchors again.","summary":"A lazy part that failed stays failed until the page's next hello, even once it loads","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/viewer-name-model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:26:52.183434Z","id":"96f44240940c1fa64105e9efc9072f147bf9e458a719255159c9bd5c73d8299f","body":{"detail":"save() runs for the Enter that saves the name and again for the Escape or blur that follows. Both pass the `next === this.saved` check before the first request answers (this.saved is set only in its .then), so the daemon receives the same rename twice and threads.ts announces the viewer twice. The stream hub ignores the repeated reconnect (web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts, `reconnect` case), so the cost is one extra request and one extra announcement per rename.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"85e6dd8736724daec080d4f5e58dedddeb783098b0c4af3e77df622a1f99526f"},"suggested_fix":"Remember the name whose request is in flight and skip a save of the same name until it answers.","summary":"A rename can send two identical PUT /api/viewers/me requests","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:38:28.460502Z","id":"69abb375e48b9757b02124e6d05bf820e28c661a3a33cc98d15d34112f5cfbd5","body":{"detail":"A page's own publish (artifact.publish) moves every open unpinned view to the new version when the view hears its version event, which carries by_page (lines 115-128). A view whose stream goes live only after that publish learns of the version from this refetch on ready, which cannot tell who published, and offers Reload in the top bar. The browser tests wait for each view's stream before a vote (streamLive in web/e2e/fixtures.ts:203).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":163},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"a91a85289e6e1f0f950c25198984f37c048a7650c830e9460e903fe262484c32"},"summary":"A view that missed a page's publish offers Reload rather than following it","supersedes":"93f0d25e0a13aee591cc4816b13d291787bc44c99eb625e669d011e2d9bbc274","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/whole-comment.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:00:38.378205Z","id":"bae1381fece00ecd9a12fcca5e56ffd7e8ccec9e4948bb1b2f0e14cfe6187725","body":{"detail":"create() repeats threads.ts createThread (the multipart POST to /api/artifacts/<aid>/threads) for the one anchor it sends, because importing createThread from this lazy chunk adds an export to the artifact entry, which is at its gzip budget (web/perf/bundle-budget.json artifact: 63988). A change to the create route's fields or error shape must be made in both.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"2a984369e8dbe835290769802543595196115f39d8db6884206a2eef93117dd1"},"suggested_fix":"Import createThread from ../threads once the entry has slack under its budget.","summary":"postWhole posts with its own copy of createThread","tags":["revisit:the artifact entry has slack under its bundle budget","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/whole-comment.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:10:14.562459Z","id":"b0a5932189ef2f713cfb216da2bae00f94bc00d4eff4d51b690ce3272bdf9a95","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ffd6520","summary":"postWhole now posts with threads.ts createThread; the local create() copy is gone. Evidence: `npx vitest run shell/src/new-comment.test.ts` passes, including the post's multipart fields (anchor, version, body, no clip) and the failure notice.","supersedes":"bae1381fece00ecd9a12fcca5e56ffd7e8ccec9e4948bb1b2f0e14cfe6187725","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/send-target.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.163118Z","id":"2dcd9e9a1ff7a7741cbc1590b739ee7dd70f018ac4d83bf86d885355bc5562fb","body":{"detail":"Failure: with the owner's agents idle and Sam's agent the most recently active live agent on the artifact, every one of the owner's thread cards reads 'Send to sam-notes' and the unsent bar 'Send 2 unsent to sam-notes': one press routes the owner's thread to Sam's agent and makes routing requests for every author Sam has not approved. Sam's browser likewise defaults to the owner's 'codex'. defaultTarget takes the first live agent in the daemon's order (most recently active) whatever its person; the label (web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte:137, the SendButton labels) shows the name alone, and 'Sam approves first' only inside the menu. Spec 2026-10-08 section 10 lists 'Your agents' first, and section 11 'Display' shows an agent's person wherever more than one person's agents appear. Seen in Chromium at 1280 and 390 px on a scratch daemon at commit f7a89d53.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":14},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"ef68ead27c64939ff056da5af4ff407035ba481532b538dfc1b9243ee69001c3"},"suggested_fix":"Default to this viewer's own most recent live agent (its person's public ID equals the viewer's; the owner's for the owner), else none (an untargeted send); keep another person's agent only when this viewer chose it. When the target is another person's agent, say so on the button ('Send to sam-notes (Sam's)') and carry 'Sam approves first' there too. Add a unit test for defaultTarget with another person's agent listed first.","summary":"The default Send target can be another person's agent, and the Send button names it without its person","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.163856Z","id":"80b94326fd39bd9aa341d7fba9df359e9050c7e3932db3c00a298a973290872d","body":{"detail":"With the owner's and Sam's agents on one artifact the top bar reads '4 open threads · codex, claude-2, sam-notes idle' with no person, and the question card of an agent named 'clax-multi-person-agent-strip-ab' reads 'claude in tmp' with the button 'Answer claude', while the inbox strip above names the same agent 'clax-multi-person-agent-strip-ab'. Spec 2026-10-08 section 11 'Display' shows agents by name, with their person wherever more than one person's agents appear.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":37},"end":{"line":45},"content_hash":"77ba540b5356c9ce6515c878d43d20a54dbca0f2a96f33a9728bcd7450ed90eb"},"summary":"The artifact view's summary line and question cards name agents without their person, or by harness","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/send-target.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.255908Z","id":"4952e1338ecf624ed58f12966f5d0faf4f6567492f3a09764484e16c69e3632f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"defaultTarget keeps only the viewer's choice; with none, ShellSidebar sends to the viewer's own most recent live agent (ownTarget, web/shell/src/view/send-menu.ts), and with only other people's agents live the Send button opens the menu (no one-press send). Labels naming another person's agent name the person ('Send to sam-notes (Sam's)'), as do menu entries ('Sam's agent'). Evidence: send-target.test.ts ownTarget tests (Sam's agent listed first: the owner's own is chosen; none for only others' agents or an unknown viewer), send-menu.test.ts and thread-owner.test.ts 'the Send target' tests, and web/e2e/agent-strip.spec.ts pass.","supersedes":"2dcd9e9a1ff7a7741cbc1590b739ee7dd70f018ac4d83bf86d885355bc5562fb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.258457Z","id":"baf1e6ed51f2ee285bc15494768f5dee627fecf5d208b1cdef98ac579055d7eb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bb547990","summary":"The top bar names another person's agents with their person where more than one person's agents appear ('sam-notes (Sam's), codex, claude idle'; withPeople in web/shell/src/view/agent-display.ts), and question cards and inbox items name an agent by its name (question and inbox views carry the agent's name; agentLabel uses it). Evidence: agent-display.test.ts and q/model.test.ts pass; target/t22/shots-r1/owner-chose-sams-agent-1280-light.png shows the summary.","supersedes":"80b94326fd39bd9aa341d7fba9df359e9050c7e3932db3c00a298a973290872d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:39:10.582430Z","id":"f24d4a1da7f7eb403fab46dcd276840221f49de288e4fdba253b654760c5ef65","body":{"detail":"Failure: a view opened without boot data (ArtifactController.start calls loadThreads, then the stream opens) whose stream 'ready' precedes the threads answer. A feedback_state for an existing thread T arrives while v.threads() lacks T, so it is kept in `early` (line 101). The load then brings T without a `thread` event, so the entry is never taken or dropped; later feedback_state events for T apply directly. At T's next `thread` event (any reply), lines 108-111 put the old early state on it, replacing the newer one, and the card shows a stale delivery label until the next state change. Reproduced with a vitest probe in the harness of web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.test.ts: ready; feedback_state since 1 for t1 (not held); threads set to t1 with since 2; feedback_state since 3; delta('open', 2, 'c2') -> t1.feedback_state.since is '1', expected '3'. The window is narrow (the first load starts before the stream opens). `ready` and `resync` clear the buffer, so it is bounded and no stale state survives a resync.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":111},"content_hash":"dfc053d7d20597096f315dfdce47fbdc8b36c392bb8dac13b1622208dccd22a3"},"suggested_fix":"Use an early state only when the thread event adds the thread (the view did not hold raw.id), and drop the entry either way.","summary":"A delivery state kept for a thread the first load then brings is applied over newer states at that thread's next thread event","tags":["review","people","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/view/artifact-stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:49:52.923117Z","id":"03f068e233fa8762f2513d42afba4247113b5914794617dfd8c1bc7a6275b2df","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7ed8fcc4","summary":"Fixed: ArtifactStream gives a kept early state only to a thread event that adds the thread, and a state applied to a held thread drops the kept one. artifact-stream.test.ts 'never applies a state kept early over a newer one once the first load brought its thread' (with and without a newer state heard) reproduces the probe (ready; state since 1 for an unheld t1; the load sets t1 since 2; state since 3; a reply's thread event) and passes, reading since 3 (or 2); without the adds-only guard both cases read since 1.","supersedes":"f24d4a1da7f7eb403fab46dcd276840221f49de288e4fdba253b654760c5ef65","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
